{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgYaAAcFiYvsxWvVVdMg5", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"hypotheses\":[{\"mechanism\":\"Regional torch.compile: compile each decoder layer in place, before FSDP2 wraps it. Elementwise, norm, softcap and MoE glue ops get fused, while compile time stays short. The whole-model compile in c5 hit the start cap.\",\"change\":{},\"patch\":\"import torch, transformers\\ntorch._dynamo.config.cache_size_limit = 64\\n_orig_init = transformers.Trainer.__init__\\ndef _patched_init(self, *a, **k):\\n    _orig_init(self, *a, **k)\\n    n = 0\\n    for mod in self.model.modules():\\n        if type(mod).__name__.endswith('DecoderLayer'):\\n            mod.compile(dynamic=False)\\n            n += 1\\n    print('[train_patches] compiled decoder layers:', n)\\ntransformers.Trainer.__init__ = _patched_init\\n\",\"edits\":[{\"file\":\"train_patches.py\",\"op\":\"replace_file\"}],\"predicted_gain_pct\":10.0,\"uncertainty_pct\":10.0,\"p_feasible\":0.6,\"change_class\":\"numerics\",\"rationale\":\"Compute is 92% of the update. On H200 the HF and MoE glue is a large non-GEMM share, and rule H12 measured compile at +24% on FSDP2. Per-layer compile reuses about 2 graphs (sliding and full layer types), so it should start well inside the cap that killed the full-model compile.\",\"memory\":{\"direction\":\"frees\",\"gib\":2.0},\"variance\":false,\"warmup_updates\":3},{\"mechanism\":\"Force SDPA (flash/cuDNN) attention instead of eager attention, which the Gemma-family HF default often selects for training.\",\"change\":{},\"patch\":\"import transformers\\n_orig_init = transformers.Trainer.__init__\\ndef _patched_init(self, *a, **k):\\n    _orig_init(self, *a, **k)\\n    m = self.model\\n    old = getattr(m.config, '_attn_implementation', None)\\n    if old != 'sdpa':\\n        if hasattr(m, 'set_attn_implementation'):\\n            m.set_attn_implementation('sdpa')\\n        else:\\n            cfgs = [m.config] + [getattr(m.config, n) for n in ('text_config',) if hasattr(m.config, n)]\\n            for c in cfgs:\\n                c._attn_implementation = 'sdpa'\\n    print('[train_patches] attention', old, '->', getattr(m.config, '_attn_implementation', None))\\ntransformers.Trainer.__init__ = _patched_init\\n\",\"edits\":[{\"file\":\"train_patches.py\",\"op\":\"replace_file\"}],\"predicted_gain_pct\":6.0,\"uncertainty_pct\":8.0,\"p_feasible\":0.7,\"change_class\":\"numerics\",\"rationale\":\"The every_n_layers=4 OOM at mbs1 implies about 3 GiB of stored activations per layer for 4k tokens. That size fits materialized eager attention scores (16 heads x 4096^2). If the job runs eager attention, SDPA removes the score materialization in both forward and recompute. If it is already SDPA, the gain is 0.\",\"memory\":{\"direction\":\"frees\",\"gib\":8.0},\"variance\":false},{\"mechanism\":\"Selective activation checkpointing: inside each checkpointed layer, save the matmul and attention outputs (torch SAC policy) and recompute only the cheap elementwise ops. This replaces full-layer recompute.\",\"change\":{},\"patch\":\"import functools, torch, transformers\\nfrom torch.utils.checkpoint import checkpoint as _ckpt, create_selective_checkpoint_contexts, CheckpointPolicy\\n_SAVE = {torch.ops.aten.mm.default, torch.ops.aten.addmm.default, torch.ops.aten.bmm.default}\\nfor _n in ('_scaled_dot_product_flash_attention', '_scaled_dot_product_cudnn_attention', '_scaled_dot_product_efficient_attention'):\\n    if hasattr(torch.ops.aten, _n):\\n        _SAVE.add(getattr(torch.ops.aten, _n).default)\\ndef _policy(ctx, op, *a, **k):\\n    return CheckpointPolicy.MUST_SAVE if op in _SAVE else CheckpointPolicy.PREFER_RECOMPUTE\\ndef _sel_checkpoint(fn, *a, **k):\\n    k.pop('every_n_layers', None)\\n    k['use_reentrant'] = False\\n    k['context_fn'] = functools.partial(create_selective_checkpoint_contexts, _policy)\\n    return _ckpt(fn, *a, **k)\\ntransformers.modeling_utils.checkpoint = _sel_checkpoint\\n\",\"edits\":[{\"file\":\"train_patches.py\",\"op\":\"replace_file\"}],\"predicted_gain_pct\":8.0,\"uncertainty_pct\":8.0,\"p_feasible\":0.5,\"change_class\":\"execution\",\"rationale\":\"Rule H7 measures full recompute at -21% and selective at -4%, so up to about 15% is recoverable. every_n_layers=2/3 measured -0.25%, which suggests that kwarg was not honored rather than recompute being free. The saved GEMM outputs are about 10-20 GiB at mbs2, which is uncertain against the remaining margin after c6.\",\"memory\":{\"direction\":\"spends\",\"gib\":18.0},\"variance\":false},{\"mechanism\":\"Grouped-GEMM MoE experts: switch the HF per-expert Python loop to the grouped_mm experts implementation when the installed transformers exposes it.\",\"change\":{},\"patch\":\"import transformers\\n_orig_init = transformers.Trainer.__init__\\ndef _patched_init(self, *a, **k):\\n    _orig_init(self, *a, **k)\\n    m = self.model\\n    if hasattr(m, 'set_experts_implementation'):\\n        try:\\n            m.set_experts_implementation('grouped_mm')\\n        except Exception as e:\\n            print('[train_patches] grouped_mm not applied:', e)\\n    elif hasattr(m.config, '_experts_implementation'):\\n        m.config._experts_implementation = 'grouped_mm'\\n    print('[train_patches] experts impl:', getattr(m.config, '_experts_implementation', None))\\ntransformers.Trainer.__init__ = _patched_init\\n\",\"edits\":[{\"file\":\"train_patches.py\",\"op\":\"replace_file\"}],\"predicted_gain_pct\":8.0,\"uncertainty_pct\":12.0,\"p_feasible\":0.35,\"change_class\":\"numerics\",\"rationale\":\"Accounting flags this model as MoE, and rule H6 says HF-implemented MoE is overhead-bound on H200: a per-expert loop launches many small GEMMs, and recompute repeats them. Grouped GEMM collapses those launches. Whether it helps depends on the transformers version supporting the hook; without it the patch is a no-op.\",\"memory\":{\"direc