{"mechanism":"Prefer cuDNN, then flash, SDPA backends: wrap scaled_dot_product_attention in sdpa_kernel(..., set_priority=True) so the fastest available fused attention is chosen on Hopper-class GPUs.","change":{},"patch":"# --- InfraRSI: prefer cuDNN / flash SDPA (append to train_patches.py) ---\ntry:\n    import torch\n    import torch.nn.functional as _F\n    from torch.nn.attention import SDPBackend, sdpa_kernel\n    _orig_sdpa = _F.scaled_dot_product_attention\n    _sdpa_order = [SDPBackend.CUDNN_ATTENTION, SDPBackend.FLASH_ATTENTION, SDPBackend.EFFICIENT_ATTENTION, SDPBackend.MATH]\n    def _sdpa_cudnn_first(*args, **kwargs):\n        with sdpa_kernel(_sdpa_order, set_priority=True):\n            return _orig_sdpa(*args, **kwargs)\n    _F.scaled_dot_product_attention = _sdpa_cudnn_first\n    torch.nn.functional.scaled_dot_product_attention = _sdpa_cudnn_first\nexcept Exception:\n    pass\n","edits":[{"file":"train_patches.py","op":"append","content":"(see patch)"}],"predicted_gain_pct":2.5,"uncertainty_pct":4.0,"p_feasible":0.6,"change_class":"numerics","memory":{"direction":"neutral","gib":0.0},"rationale":"Experience constraint B8 lists cuDNN as the fastest SDPA backend. At seq 4096 with 16 heads, attention forward, backward and its recompute are a real part of the compute phase. Torch's default priority does not pick cuDNN first. The fallback order keeps every backend that is currently reachable, so it should not crash where the current setup does not."},
